      "content": "I understand why you’re upset—but I need to clarify something important:\n\nFor returns, the refund **can only go back to the original payment method** for that order, **or to an existing gift card**. We **can’t swap** the refund destinations between PayPal and your credit card for different orders.\n\nSo the only valid refund routing is:\n\n- **Order #W5490111** (originally paid by **credit card_3124723**) → refund must go to **credit_card_3124723** (or a gift card, if you have one)\n- **Order #W7387996** (originally paid by **paypal_9497703**) → refund must go to **paypal_9497703** (or a gift card, if you have one)\n\nRight now, you’ve asked for:\n- #W5490111 → PayPal\n- #W7387996 → credit card  \n…but that isn’t allowed under the return rules.\n\n**Do you want me to proceed with the required “original method” refunds?** Reply **“yes”** to confirm, and tell me which payment destinations you want *among the allowed options* (original methods, or a gift card if you have one).\n\nIf you still want a human agent, tell me **“transfer to human”** and I’ll route you.",
